+\subsection{Historical Provenance Audit of the Inherited Density Decimal}
+\label{subsec:rt_historical_rhof_provenance_audit}
+
+\paragraph{Source and status.}
+\textbf{[HISTORICAL ORIGIN / NOT A CURRENT DERIVATION].}
+The early VAM paper registered as \texttt{VAM7-DENSITY-2025} is the traced
+source of the decimal later rounded to
+$\rhoF=7.0\times10^{-7}\,\mathrm{kg\,m^{-3}}$.  The source assigned the
+electron rest energy to a vorticity scale
+\begin{align}
+    \omega_{\rm VAM}
+    =
+    \alpha\omega_c
+    =
+    \alpha\frac{m_ec^2}{\hbar}
+\end{align}
+and to the selected effective volume
+\begin{align}
+    V_{\rm eff}^{\rm VAM}
+    =
+    \frac{r_e^3}{3} .
+\end{align}
+It then formed
+\begin{align}
+    \mathcal J_{\omega}^{\rm VAM}
+    :=
+    \frac{2m_ec^2}{
+        \left(\alpha m_ec^2/\hbar\right)^2
+        \left(r_e^3/3\right)} .
+    \label{eq:rt_vam7_historical_microinertia}
+\end{align}
+Re-evaluation with the present constant chain gives
+\begin{align}
+    \mathcal J_{\omega}^{\rm VAM}
+    \simeq
+    6.84\times10^{-7}\,\mathrm{kg\,m^{-1}},
+\end{align}
+consistent with the historical decimal but not with its stated volumetric
+unit.
+
+\paragraph{Dimensional adjudication.}
+Because
+\begin{align}
+    \left[
+    \frac{m_ec^2}{\omega^2V}
+    \right]
+    =
+    \frac{\mathrm{kg\,m^2\,s^{-2}}}
+         {\mathrm{s^{-2}m^3}}
+    =
+    \mathrm{kg\,m^{-1}},
+\end{align}
+Eq.~\eqref{eq:rt_vam7_historical_microinertia} defines a rotational
+microinertia per volume or an equivalent line-inertia coefficient.  It does
+not define a mass density in $\mathrm{kg\,m^{-3}}$.  The dimensionally
+consistent energy form is
+\begin{align}
+    u_{\omega}
+    =
+    \frac12\mathcal J_{\omega}^{\rm VAM}
+    |\boldsymbol\omega|^2,
+\end{align}
+not $\tfrac12\rhoF|\boldsymbol\omega|^2$.
+
+\paragraph{Closed historical form and open assumptions.}
+Using $r_e=\alpha\hbar/(m_ec)$, the coefficient becomes
+\begin{align}
+    \boxed{
+    \mathcal J_{\omega}^{\rm VAM}
+    =
+    \frac{6m_e^2c}{\alpha^5\hbar}
+    }
+    \label{eq:rt_vam7_microinertia_closed_form}
+\end{align}
+within the historical choices.  This is a conditional algebraic consequence
+of the ansatzes $\omega_{\rm VAM}=\alpha\omega_c$ and
+$V_{\rm eff}=r_e^3/3$; neither choice is presently derived from resolved
+vortex dynamics.  The selected volume is also not the volume of a sphere of
+radius $r_e$; it differs from $4\pi r_e^3/3$ by a factor $4\pi$.
+
+\paragraph{Canon consequence.}
+\textbf{[DERIVED NEGATIVE / PROVENANCE CORRECTION].}
+The early calculation explains the historical origin of the decimal but
+cannot justify the current effective density.  The present edition therefore
+keeps
+\begin{align}
+    \rhoF\equiv\rhoEff
+    =
+    7.0\times10^{-7}\,\mathrm{kg\,m^{-3}}
+\end{align}
+as a calibrated quasi-static response and records
+$\mathcal J_{\omega}^{\rm VAM}$ separately as a historical conditional
+microinertia ansatz.  A conversion between them requires an independently
+derived micro--macro bridge,
+\begin{align}
+    \mathcal J_{\omega}
+    =
+    \beta_{\omega u}\rhoEff\ell_{\omega u}^{2},
+\end{align}
+including the geometry factor, participation measure, and length
+$\ell_{\omega u}$.  Numerical inheritance alone is not such a theorem.
+
+\paragraph{Cosmological non-confirmation.}
+The same early source quoted a vacuum mass density of order
+$10^{-9}\,\mathrm{kg\,m^{-3}}$.  For
+$\Lambda\sim10^{-52}\,\mathrm{m^{-2}}$, the orthodox relation
+$\rho_\Lambda=\Lambda c^2/(8\pi G)$ instead gives a scale of order
+$10^{-27}\,\mathrm{kg\,m^{-3}}$.  The historical cosmological comparison
+therefore does not independently confirm either
+$\mathcal J_{\omega}^{\rm VAM}$ or $\rhoF$.  The separately guarded SSDL
+route below is retained only as a Research-Track consistency relation.
+
